   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Increased capacity of Member States to improve social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">- 14 Master trainers from Council of Indian Employers and 11 central trade unions in India built capacity for organising in India&apos;s informal economy and advancing social dialogue.
- Tripartite constituents in India availed access to distance learning material on collective bargaining, workplace cooperation and grievance handling translated into Hindi as a basis for self-paced learning.
- Officials of Mumbai Port Authority and trade unions of Port of Mumbai jointly developed an action plan for grievance handling procedures for the Port of Mumbai
 - The ILO organized a bipartite the training of master trainers on a toolkit to promote social dialogue in India&#x2019;s informal economy. This was undertaken in partnership with an implementing partner &#x2013; Sampark Livelihoods Promotion Trust on 14-16 September 2023. The trainers developed their respective action plans to take forward training in their respective organisations.

- The ILO supported the translation and access to the distance learning material on collective bargaining and grievance handling through a collaboration with ITC-ILO.

- The ILO facilitated a self-assessment of the existing grievance handling procedures and supported the development of grievance handling procedures for the Port of Mumbai on 1-3 February 2023.</narrative>
   </description>
