  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Increased capacity of Member States to improve social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">i)	The Labour Commissionerate of the Kerala Government carried out a self-assessment diagnostic of the Labour Department&#x2019;s dispute resolution systems and procedures, using LABOURLAW&#x2019;s self-assessment diagnostic tool. As a result, the Commissionerate adopted an action plan identifying a series of actions for enhancing the effectiveness of the Labour Department&#x2019;s dispute resolution functions.
ii)	The Labour Department of Telangana Government carried out a successful self-assessment diagnostic of the Labour Department&#x2019;s dispute resolution systems and procedures. The Commissionerate then adopted an action plan identifying a series of actions for enhancing the effectiveness of the Labour Department&#x2019;s dispute resolution functions. 
iii)	14 Master trainers from the Council of Indian Employers and 11 central trade unions in India built capacity for organising in India&#x2019;s informal economy and advancing social dialogue. 
iv)	Officials of the Mumbai Port Authority and trade unions of the Port of Mumbai jointly developed an action plan for grievance handling procedures for the Port of Mumbai.
v )	In partnership with the ITC-ILO, the V V Giri National Labour Institute (VVGNLI) and the Kerala Institute for Labour and Employment (KILE) co-developed and piloted a short-term certificate course in the areas of labour relations and social dialogue. A total of 50 tripartite constituency representatives completed the course. Both the national institutions will include this course as part of their regular training calendar in the coming year, with the certificate being co-accredited by the ITC and the respective national institutions. i)	The ILO facilitated the self-assessment workshop and development of the action plan through a workshop held on 19-20 June in Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala. 
ii)	The ILO facilitated the self-assessment workshop and development of the action plan through a workshop held on 15-16 June in Hyderabad, Telangana. 
iii)	The ILO organized the training of master trainers through an implementing partner &#x2013; Sampark Livelihoods Promotion Trust on 14-16 September 2023. 
iv)	The ILO facilitated a self-assessment of the existing grievance handling procedures and supported the development of the action plan for the Port of Mumbai on 1-3 February 2023. 
v) The ILO facilitated the partnership of the ITC with VVGNLI and KILE to develop and implement this course. ILO also facilitated the full participation of the first pilot batch.</narrative>
